  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q15-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q15-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x+3}{x-1}\\times\\frac{x-1}{x-5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x+3}{x-5}$, $x\\ne1,5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x+3}{x-1}\\times\\frac{x-1}{x-5}&=\\frac{(x+3)(x-1)}{(x-1)(x-5)}\\\\\\frac{x+3}{x-1}\\times\\frac{x-1}{x-5}&=\\frac{x+3}{x-5}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\ne1,5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q16-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{4p+8}{4p-8}\\times\\frac{p-2}{p+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$, $p\\ne-2,2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4p+8}{4p-8}\\times\\frac{p-2}{p+2}&=\\frac{4(p+2)}{4(p-2)}\\times\\frac{p-2}{p+2}\\\\\\frac{4p+8}{4p-8}\\times\\frac{p-2}{p+2}&=1\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $p\\ne-2,2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q17-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2x^2-6x}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5x+10}{x-2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{10x(x-3)}{(x+2)(x-2)}$, $x\\ne-2,2$.\n\nFactorise both numerators and cancel one factor of $x+2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x^2-6x}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5x+10}{x-2}&=\\frac{2x(x-3)}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5(x+2)}{x-2}\\\\\\frac{2x^2-6x}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5x+10}{x-2}&=\\frac{10x(x-3)}{(x+2)(x-2)}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\ne-2,2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q18-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x^2-4x}{5x+10}\\div\\frac{x-4}{5x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x^2}{x+2}$, $x\\ne-2,0,4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-4x}{5x+10}\\div\\frac{x-4}{5x}&=\\frac{x^2-4x}{5x+10}\\times\\frac{5x}{x-4}\\\\\\frac{x^2-4x}{5x+10}\\div\\frac{x-4}{5x}&=\\frac{x(x-4)}{5(x+2)}\\times\\frac{5x}{x-4}\\\\\\frac{x^2-4x}{5x+10}\\div\\frac{x-4}{5x}&=\\frac{x^2}{x+2}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\ne-2,0,4$. The divisor must be defined and nonzero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q19-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{6b-12}{(b-2)^2}\\div\\frac{b-2}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{18}{(b-2)^2}$, $b\\ne2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6b-12}{(b-2)^2}\\div\\frac{b-2}{3}&=\\frac{6b-12}{(b-2)^2}\\times\\frac3{b-2}\\\\\\frac{6b-12}{(b-2)^2}\\div\\frac{b-2}{3}&=\\frac{6(b-2)}{(b-2)^2}\\times\\frac3{b-2}\\\\\\frac{6b-12}{(b-2)^2}\\div\\frac{b-2}{3}&=\\frac{18}{(b-2)^2}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $b\\ne2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q20-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{4p-4}{(p-3)(p-1)}\\div\\frac{p-3}{4-p}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4(4-p)}{(p-3)^2}$, $p\\ne1,3,4$.\n\nMultiply by the reciprocal, then factorise and cancel $p-1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4p-4}{(p-3)(p-1)}\\div\\frac{p-3}{4-p}&=\\frac{4p-4}{(p-3)(p-1)}\\times\\frac{4-p}{p-3}\\\\\\frac{4p-4}{(p-3)(p-1)}\\div\\frac{p-3}{4-p}&=\\frac{4(p-1)}{(p-3)(p-1)}\\times\\frac{4-p}{p-3}\\\\\\frac{4p-4}{(p-3)(p-1)}\\div\\frac{p-3}{4-p}&=\\frac{4(4-p)}{(p-3)^2}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $p\\ne1,3,4$. The divisor must be defined and nonzero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      }
    ]
  },
